  "strategy": "**1. Approach and Rationale**\n\nThe current method uses function minimization to optimize h(x). While effective, it often gets trapped in local optima. This hybrid approach combines global exploration with local exploitation:\n\n- **Global Component**: Uses NSGA-II, a multi-objective evolutionary algorithm, to discover solutions that may be geometrically optimal.\n- **Local Component**: Follows by gradient-based refinement using SLSQP to polish promising candidates.\n- **Dimensionality Reduction**: Leverages the 2-periodicity constraint to reduce solution space by half, accelerating convergence.\n- **Population-Based Search**: Maintains a Pareto front to explore different trade-offs between minimization objectives.\n- **Timely Termination**: Allocates time budgets for different stages of the search.\n\nThe core bottleneck addressed is premature convergence to suboptimal solutions by introducing a synergistic global-local optimization scheme.\n\n**2. Mathematical Specification**\n\nWe minimize **C\u2085** = max\u2096 \u2a0d[0,2] h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx while satisfying:\n- 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 for all x \u2208 [0,2]\n- \u2a0d\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1 (implies \u2a0d\u2080\u00b9 h(x) dx = 0.5 due to periodicity)\n\n**Variables**: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f (step function interpolation points)\n\n**Operators**:\n- $\\text{NSGA-II}$: Niched Sorting and Crowding Distance\n- $\\text{SLSQP}$: Local minimization with box and equality constraints\n\n**Representation**: Each chromosome (h-vector) is encoded with period constraints via:\n  h\u2082\u208d\u208e = h\u208d, where ' denotes replication\n\n**3. Implementation Procedure**\n\n**i. Input Setup**  \n- Validate `initial_h_values` (if supplied) and set grid size `n`\n- Hyperparameters:  \n  - \u03bc = 100 (NSGA-II population size)\n  - \u03b5 = 0.8 (mutation rate)\n  - \u03c3 = 2.0 (initial decomposition)\n  - T_max = 600 (time limit per grid)\n  - T_refine = 300 (local refinement budget)\n\n**ii. NSGA-II Initialization**  \n1. Generate initial solutions:\n   - Single parent: upscale `initial_h_values` via `project_to_feasible`\n   - Remainder: 99 random points projected to [0,1] and normalized\n2. Assign fitness scores (Pareto ranking + crowding distance)\n\n**iii. Evolutionary Loop**  \nFor each generation until deadline:\n   A. **Mutation**  \n      For each chromosome, perform polynomial decomposition:  \n      $p_{\\text{new}} = \u03bc + \\sigma \\cdot p_{\\text{old}}$ (with adaptive \u03c3 decay)\n   \n   B. **Hypervolume Calculation**  \n      Use ParEGO dimensionality reduction with decomposition parameter \u03bc_d\n   \n   C. **Selection**  \n      Tournament selection based on dominated points + crowding distance\n\n**iv. Local Refinement**  \nAfter \u2153 of cycles, apply SLSQP to top 5 solutions:\n```python\nopt_h = minimize_erdos(local_h.copy(), max_iter=400)\nreturn opt_h\n```\n\n**v. Multi-Grid Expansion**  \nIf plateau detected (best rank unchanged >3 generations), double grid size:\n```python\nn_new = 2 * n\nh_new = downscale(h_opt, n_new)\ncontinue search\n```\n\n**4. Search Choices and Use Cases**\n\nPrimary tuning parameters:\n- `\u03bc` (population size) \u2208 [50, 200] if time < 300s\n- `\u03c3` (mutation variance) \u2208 [0.5, 3] (decreases by factor 0.95 daily)\n- `\u03c1` (Pareto sharing) \u2208 [0.4, 0.9] \n\nFor grid independence from `initial_h_values`:\n```python\nn = 64  # default safe fallback\n```\n\n**5. Compute Budget & Runtime**\n\nDominant costs:\n- Correlation: O(n\u00b2) per h-vector\n- NSGA-II dominates initial phases\n- Local refinement: O(n) per solution\n\nComplexity profile:\n- n=64: \u224850s per population cycle\n- n=128: \u2248200s per cycle (cost quadruples)\n- n=256: Infeasible within budget\n\n**6. Validation & Contract**\n\nCandidates pass four checks:\n1. $h \u2208 [0,1]\u207f$\n2. $\\sum h = n/2$ (projected)\n3. $C\u2085 = \\text{evaluate\\_erdos\\_solution}(h)$ \n4. Hypervolume improvement tracking\n\nReturned triple $(h\\_values, c5\\_bound, n\\_points)$ guarantees:\n- Minimal C\u2085 not greater than any candidate\n- No Divergent progression dimensions\n- Timely termination by grid/information\n- Project-safe interpolation\n\nSources: NSGA-II, SLSQP, mismatched grid technologies\n\nImplementation takes 300-500 lines (separately scalable)",
